There was already existing research, that already showed how AI could help to develop games in all the imaginable realms. Still, there is still a space within those lines:
Applications of AI for development of adaptive game worlds responding to real time player feedback. 
Artistic integrity of games: Automated AI will be able to work alongside human design to find a balance between the work of automated AI and input of human designers for creative levels.
Scaling the AI which would work both for 2D and 3D games. 
The algorithm itself may not be as complicated in ensuring that you win consistently. 
Some games that are entirely or partially built using AI include: 
Project AURA: The nature of this creation is to use AI to control NPC behaviors and dynamic weather systems to make the immersion. 
Watch Dogs: Ubisoft’s Legion uses AI to give special NPCs their schedules, personalities, and interaction. Procedural generation has been a splash in the water throughout Cyberpunk 2077’s development, being used to create a living breathing environment which features a dense, dynamic city. 
Electronic Arts' The Sims 4 uses behavioral simulations (or better, use of AI) as they can distinguish how NPCs can respond to the actions of a player and their environment.
